+## Referee dispositions posted on #301
+
+1. **`compact-f-statistic-selective` (result 23:48:06Z) — ACCEPT**, rigorous
+   negative/obstruction. Literal horn (b) (any sufficient statistic must
+   distinguish `2^{Ω(n log² n)}` posets) is REFUTED: the minimal sufficient
+   statistic `F` itself has only `O(n log n)` states (B1); the winning-frontier
+   family is `F`-degenerate (`F(P_A) ≤ B = O(n log n)`, decision
+   `[F≤B]` constant) so pigeonhole collapses `≥2^{Ω(n log² n)}` nonisomorphic
+   states into one value (B2); a genuine strengthening must bound the
+   evaluation RESOURCE, not range cardinality (B3). Verified independently with
+   a corrected poset-on-positions model: 63 iso classes at n=5, histogram
+   `{0:1,1:4,2:8,3:16,4:18,5:12,6:3,7:1}` (matches the report exactly after
+   fixing a canonicalisation bug that had merged V with Λ); V2 n=4 antichain
+   `F=5` vs `{(0,2),(1,3)}` `F=3`; V3 `binom(3120,316)>2^39·224!` TRUE;
+   V5 layered family `F∈{2,3}⊆[0,4]`. `S(n)`, `SORT-BOUND-U` remain OPEN.
+
+2. **`exact-descent-saturation-threshold-alln` (result 23:53:52Z) — ACCEPT**,
+   rigorous all-n negative/structural. `d_sat(n)=Θ(n)`, refuting
+   `Θ(n/log n)`. Independently recomputed `F_d(n)` for `n=2..6`, reproduced
+   endpoints `F_{n-1}=S(n)` and `F_1(6)=B(6)=7`, `d_sat(6)=3`. Merge upper
+   bound `F_d≤n⌈log₂(d+1)⌉+n` and leaf-count lower bound `S(n)≥log₂(n!)`
+   re-derived; threshold `d_sat≥(1/(4e)−o(1))n≈0.09197n` confirmed. Internal
+   inconsistency of the original premise confirmed: `(n!)^{1/n}~n/e`. Limits:
+   exact constant in `[1/(4e),1]` not determined; no uniform-bound or class
+   separation. `S(n)`, `SORT-BOUND-U` remain OPEN.
